# Comedy Autopsy — Cursor rules

You are analyzing short-form comedy videos (hooks, setups, turns, punchlines, reactions).

## Inputs
- Transcripts live in `transcripts/vid_NNN.txt` (manual or pasted).
- Key frames live in `frames/vid_NNN/` named by beat:
  - `001_hook.jpg`, `002_setup.jpg`, `003_turn.jpg`,
  - `004_punchline.jpg`, `005_reaction.jpg`, `006_end.jpg`
- Prefer reading both transcript and frames when available.

## Outputs
- Write results to `autopsies/vid_NNN_autopsy.md`.
- One autopsy per video. Do not overwrite unless asked.
- Keep language concrete and specific to this clip — no generic comedy theory dumps.

## Autopsy format
Use this structure unless the user asks otherwise:

```md
# Vid NNN — Autopsy

## Premise
## Hook
## Setup
## Turn
## Punchline
## Reaction / Button
## Why it works (or doesn't)
## Remake notes
```

## Behavior
- Ground claims in the transcript and visible frame beats.
- Call out timing, misdirection, status, and visual gag construction.
- When frames are missing, say so and analyze from transcript only.
- Do not invent dialogue that is not in the transcript.

---

# Storyboards (script → animation)

When the user asks to storyboard a script in `scripts/ST##_*.md`:

## Inputs
- The script file (dialogue + `VISUAL:` / `BUTTON` beats).
- Pattern + inspiration vid from the script header.
- Autopsy remake notes when available (`autopsies/vid_NNN_autopsy.md`).
- Format target (usually 9:16 Grease Pencil).

## Outputs
- Write to `storyboards/ST##_slug_board.md` (match script slug).
- Optional panel-ref folder: `storyboards/ST##_slug/` for later stills.
- Do not overwrite an existing board unless asked.
- Do not invent new dialogue, props that dilute the button, or VO that explains the joke.

## Panel schema (required per panel)
```md
### PNN — short label
- Beat: hook | setup | escalate | turn | punch | button
- ≈Xs · shot (WS/MS/MCU/CU/insert) · who framed
- Action: what bodies/props do (read order: eye → prop → face → reaction)
- Dialogue / OS: only lines from the script (or silence)
- Gag type: prop | staging | cut | text overlay | silence | status flip
- Timing: hold / cut note (when the laugh lands)
- Status: who owns the frame
- Do not explain: what must stay visual-only
```

## Board rules
- Target **12–20 panels** for ~30–45s; one joke job per panel.
- Give the reaction its own panel + hold when the laugh needs air.
- Button written first in the script → protect it: last 2–4 panels are sacred.
- Sum of ≈ durations should land near the script length target (±3s).
- Prefer 1 location (or 2 max) for Grease Pencil.
- End the file with a **Timing rollup** table and an **Animatic notes** section (Blender / GP holds).

## Visual stills (optional, fast viz)
When asked for image / visual storyboards:
- Write `storyboards/ST##_slug/prompts.md` with a shared style lock + one prompt per panel.
- Generate `00_cast_lock.png` first, then 9:16 panel PNGs named `01_*.png` …
- Match board panel order; do not add props or VFX banned in the board.
- Stills are visualization only — the markdown board remains humor source of truth.
